    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When Christopher Nolan cast Lupita Nyong'o for his Homer film, it sparked a public debate online. Defenders argued the story should be open to all, while others made a public accusation that the film production was erasing European history. The conflict has turned into a cultural controversy, making it harder for everyday fans to just enjoy a movie without getting caught in the crossfire.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
